{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings","id":1011669,"title":"Non-Abusive/Empathetic True Fae...even possible? (and Wyrd 10 Changelings)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-03T14:33:22-08:00","id":1011669,"title":"Non-Abusive/Empathetic True Fae...even possible? (and Wyrd 10 Changelings)","content":"Assuming that &quot;Becoming Nightmares&quot; was considered and if Wyrd 10 Changelings do become True Fae, the greatest question of all that what happens to their &quot;sense of themselves&quot; assuming that everysingle True Fae are abusive slave owning monsters?<br /> <br /> Or rather is it possible to have a Empathetic/Non-Abusive True Fae especially if they happen to be Wyrd 10 and zero Clarity Changelings or what happens if they have Wyrd 10 and Clarity 10? Basically what I have in mind is somehow introducing the Firstborn from DA: Fae which is perhaps what Wyrd 10 Changelings can potentially become?<br /> <br /> Well to be honest, my only problem with &quot;Becoming Nightmares&quot; and making the True Fae actually ex Changelings not only removes the mystery of what True Fae actually are but also it becomes problematic the fact it becomes a meaningless hopeless game that you'll eventually going to end up being one of your abusers you've been fighting against so why increase your Wyrd at all? Unless Empathetic/Non-Abusive &quot;True Fae&quot; are entirely possible and actually exist (i.e. C:tL equivalent to the Firstborn Fae from DA: Fae) because if not then this problem would persist until then.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:49:54-08:00","id":1011675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings#post1011669\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but also it becomes problematic the fact it becomes a meaningless hopeless game that you'll eventually going to end up being one of your abusers you've been fighting against so why increase your Wyrd at all?</div> </div> </div> </div>How? There's no inevitability to it. A Changeling can grow old and die if they want, nothings forcing them to become True Fae.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:54:06-08:00","id":1011679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011675#post1011675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How? There's no inevitability to it. A Changeling can grow old and die if they want, nothings forcing them to become True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet what if I want to increase in Wyrd and ultimately become immortal as a alternative to Vampirism?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 05:57 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T14:59:10-08:00","id":1011683,"title":"","content":"I imagine that there <i>are </i>True Fae who are decent people out there somewhere but they're probably not kidnapping humans by force and even if they have changelings in their realm they're could be people who were rescued from horrible situations or who wanted to come for some other reason. If you're in a magically wonderful land where you're not being horrifically abused as a lamppost you may not want to leave- and if you do then you'd probably be a loyalist who helps your nice Keeper out when they ask for help with things. Logically, changelings who actively try to escape from raging assholes who take a huge number of mortals every year are going to outnumber the few who decide to leave the perfection and wonder of an Arcadian realm that isn't trying to turn them into a lamp post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:18:55-08:00","id":1011691,"title":"","content":"Some Gentry aren't so bad. They take a child so they can raise one. Or to play games with them, or to nurture their talent as their musician. The True Fae doesn't always see what they do as a bad thing. Helping a musician improve is hardly evil after all, giving them a venue to play, and practice and perform is a good thing for them. They do not see it as slavery they see it as helping out the mortal. Perception is a powerful force after all. Taking a child away from a neglectful parent to dote upon them and raise them, where is the harm in that. Taking a broken hearted soul and making them your lover so they can heal and get over their heart break isn't wrong.<br /> <br /> It's all in perspective, many Gentry likely think they are helping not harming.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/21.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/600-haplesswithdice","name":"HaplessWithDice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar600_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1234"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:27:33-08:00","id":1011696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011679#post1011679\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yet what if I want to increase in Wyrd and ultimately become immortal as a alternative to Vampirism?</div> </div> </div> </div>Then you're out of luck. You can't have both. You either live and die as a human, or live forever as a True Fae. Pick.<br /> <br /> That's not a meaningless decision.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:37:21-08:00","id":1011699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011696#post1011696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then you're out of luck. You can't have both. You either live and die as a human, or live forever as a True Fae. Pick.<br /> <br /> That's not a meaningless decision.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well say if I pick the True Fae decision, I wonder how they can maintain being themselves (or the the essence of you) especially if it's possible for True Fae to live in our world but their Arcadian Realm is more of a 'backup realm' for them that they sometimes frequent trips in and out of their realms? Like sometimes they use their Arcadian Realms to storage things in there or sometimes taking people in their realms for shelter or different reasons?<br /> <br /> I guess it's possible that the more benevolent True Fae are Wyrd 10 Changelings?<br /> <br /> I think there has to be some way to port the Firstborn Fae from DA: Fae which they can be Gentry that are playable. Or basically a Gentry that behaves just like a DA: Fae Firstborn which the only alien aspect is that their loss of direction of time since they're timeless beings as opposed to a Vampire's immortality which Vampires do have a sense of time while True Fae don't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 06:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:41:17-08:00","id":1011700,"title":"","content":"Oh boy, another &quot;why does the game have to [central component of the game]?&quot; argument. I love these threads.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:51:54-08:00","id":1011705,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011700#post1011700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh boy, another &quot;why does the game have to [central component of the game]?&quot; argument. I love these threads.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since sometimes the &quot;Central Component&quot; can make the game more rigid and constraining to that certain theme (therefore making what Micheal posted a meaningless decision if constrained within the game's originally written themes) despite the fact the game is about playing as Faeries.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 06:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T15:56:02-08:00","id":1011706,"title":"","content":"It's not about playing as Faeries, it's about playing a changeling.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/downloads/Backer%20Badge%20small.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/178-michael","name":"Michael","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar178_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3560"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:10:46-08:00","id":1011714,"title":"","content":"A True Fae could randomly decide to be helpful or even nice for a while. They might even take a few centuries to get bored of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:11:06-08:00","id":1011715,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Michael</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011706#post1011706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not about playing as Faeries, it's about playing a changeling.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aren't Changelings techincally Faeries after all?<br /> <br /> Then again, if playing C:tL is about playing as a Changeling and if your Changeling reaches Wyrd 10 and becomes a True Fae, does this mean you have to hand over your character sheet to make a new character? If so then it kinda contradicts what you said since the only choice is to grow old and die and if you ever attempted to reach immortality status (being True Fae) then you pretty much 'loose the game' which therefore forcing you to stay low powered and living in fear as it's logical conclusion due to the fact that C:tL is about playing as a Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:19:24-08:00","id":1011721,"title":"","content":"I'm not adverse to the idea. The point is that I also believe it can't last and change according to the whims of Wyrd, possibly looking quite random to outside observers. To me, a friendly true Fae is like a friendly tiger in the wild: possible, but won't be surprised if one day somebody is bit.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages was and is great, but Changeling's True Fae are..can we say unpredictable? On a large-scope perspective, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:25:52-08:00","id":1011725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cinder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011721#post1011721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not adverse to the idea. The point is that I also believe it can't last and change according to the whims of Wyrd, possibly looking quite random to outside observers. To me, a friendly true Fae is like a friendly tiger in the wild: possible, but won't be surprised if one day somebody is bit.<br /> <br /> Dark Ages was and is great, but Changeling's True Fae are..can we say unpredictable? On a large-scope perspective, at least.</div> </div> </div> </div>If that's the case then it seems becoming True Fae in Lost is a meaningless decision then contrary to what Micheal said if you're going be unpredictable and very dangerous and it actually does sound like the only choice you have to maintain your humanity or the sense of yourself is to grow and die which also means staying low powered and living in fear until then as it's logical conclusion despite the fact I heard that it's not the 'spirit of the game' but if you take the game's themes into account, then the only logical conclusion says otherwise. Unless there's a way to port the Firstborn from DA: Fae though...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 07:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:28:33-08:00","id":1011727,"title":"","content":"It's not just wyrd 10, by the way. It also requires clarity 0. And is basically optional on the part of the player. Essentially a changeling will only become a True Fae if their empathy and compassion is already gone. That's just one of the prerequisites for the transformation.<br /> <br /> Also in the second edition previews you don't actually need to become a true fae to become immortal. Wyrd 10 does it on it's own, there's a one dot merit that doubles your wyrd for this purpose, putting the requirement at 5, and a 2 dot merit that just goes &quot;fuck it, aging in for chumps&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:37:31-08:00","id":1011731,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011727#post1011727\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's not just wyrd 10, by the way. It also requires clarity 0. And is basically optional on the part of the player. Essentially a changeling will only become a True Fae if their empathy and compassion is already gone. That's just one of the prerequisites for the transformation.</div> </div> </div> </div>So there you go, if the removal of empathy and compassion are prerequisites to becoming True Fae, then I guess it renders the entire point of this thread moot if Empathetic/Non-Abusive True Fae are technically impossible under this conclusion.<br /> <br /> But at least it's a plus sign that Wyrd 10 gives you immortality but it seems due to this knowledge now, looks like becoming True Fae is the biggest risk if you want to preserve your compassion and empathy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 07:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:45:13-08:00","id":1011735,"title":"","content":"True Fae can have some form of compassion - the problem it's their idea of compassion. They could consider giving their subjects mana from the sky as much compassion as leaving one alive after it failed to bring you your desired goblin fruit...and after they've been tortured for their failure. Gentry consider their own feelings to be what everyone feels, or at least all that matters, and anything different is either an aberration, a punishable act or simply curiosity...or all three. Anything that is not an equal to them has no time sacrificed to them. As noted in the Fairest entry, many of them were given an offer by the True Fae they ended up serving, and that offer could be made as much as an offer of compassion as it could be a cruel trick. After all, what could be better than serving you, a godly being with a fantastical realm and plenty of others who serve under you in one whole community?<br /> <br /> Again, the problem is that the Gentry do not, and indeed <i>cannot</i> understand others - in first edition at least, understanding others outright banishes them from Arcadia. To understand something lower than oneself is to become lower than oneself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T16:57:28-08:00","id":1011744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011735#post1011735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Fae can have some form of compassion - the problem it's their idea of compassion. They could consider giving their subjects mana from the sky as much compassion as leaving one alive after it failed to bring you your desired goblin fruit...and after they've been tortured for their failure. Gentry consider their own feelings to be what everyone feels, or at least all that matters, and anything different is either an aberration, a punishable act or simply curiosity...or all three. Anything that is not an equal to them has no time sacrificed to them. As noted in the Fairest entry, many of them were given an offer by the True Fae they ended up serving, and that offer could be made as much as an offer of compassion as it could be a cruel trick. After all, what could be better than serving you, a godly being with a fantastical realm and plenty of others who serve under you in one whole community?<br /> <br /> Again, the problem is that the Gentry do not, and indeed <i>cannot</i> understand others - in first edition at least, understanding others outright banishes them from Arcadia. To understand something lower than oneself is to become lower than oneself.</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess all of this only confirms that becoming True Fae is after all out of the question.<br /> <br /> Unless if it's possible to once again have the Firstborn from DA: Fae in C:tL which would be a considerably a a more nicer outcome than Gentry.<br /> <br /> Since we could have it where Firstborn are the True Fae that still does have empathy/compassion in them or basically they're still themselves despite the fact they also have Arcadian Realms which are realms in the Mysts being it's counterpart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-03-2016, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:15:32-08:00","id":1011748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011744#post1011744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess all of this only confirms that becoming True Fae is after all out of the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>They could do so in first edition.<br /> <br /> It doesn't have to be the only source of True Fae, however.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-03T17:32:14-08:00","id":1011754,"title":"","content":"He means for a PC.<br /> <br /> That said, there <i>are</i> rules for playing them in the back of Equinox Road. It's basically a separate mini-game though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T08:31:53-08:00","id":1012019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011744#post1011744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess all of this only confirms that becoming True Fae is after all out of the question.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh, it's only out of the question if you don't want to play unempathetic characters. It's certainly assumed that players don't typically portray Genrty, but if you really want to, there's no reason you can't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011744#post1011744\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unless if it's possible to once again have the Firstborn from DA: Fae in C:tL which would be a considerably a a more nicer outcome than Gentry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Of course it's <i>possible</i>. It's a tabletop RPG, anything is possible. You can play as Luke Skywalker in a Changeling game if that floats your boat. It won't really fit the themes, mood, or setting of the game, but if you want to play that way that's your prerogative.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:10:42-08:00","id":1012053,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012019#post1012019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh, it's only out of the question if you don't want to play unempathetic characters. It's certainly assumed that players don't typically portray Genrty, but if you really want to, there's no reason you can't.</div> </div> </div> </div>And I do want to play empathetic characters and since becoming True Fae is out the question, I guess staying low powered (as in staying very low wyrd) and living in fear while dying old is the only option then?<br /> <br /> I guess it means that I have to become immortal through other means that doesn't involve the wyrd or faerie? Which means I have to use this <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Immortals\" target=\"_blank\">book</a> instead to look for other options if Changelings can follow through with it but if so, not only it won't feel the same but feels that being a Changeling is not even worth it afterall so why be one at all in the first place?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012019#post1012019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Of course it's <i>possible</i>. It's a tabletop RPG, anything is possible. You can play as Luke Skywalker in a Changeling game if that floats your boat. It won't really fit the themes, mood, or setting of the game, but if you want to play that way that's your prerogative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know this is a vieled insult but Luke Skywalker is just taking things too far since I believe that things in the game world have to make sense to the setting but then again though, the themes can restrict other possibilities that can along with it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011754#post1011754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He means for a PC.<br /> <br /> That said, there <i>are</i> rules for playing them in the back of Equinox Road. It's basically a separate mini-game though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes that's what I was referring to as PCs and if it's minigame then why bother? I guess it's a meaningless choice after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-04-2016, 01:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:40:32-08:00","id":1012066,"title":"","content":"Something about the World/Chronicles of Darkness, Veindark, is that immortality is really not something one can attain without a significant sacrifice, either bodily, spiritually, mentally or all three. Immortals usually require sacrifices to be made for them (such as bathing in the blood of others, stealing their organs or their entire body), and if they don't it usually makes them either a target for other, less scrupilous immortals or comes with a hideous downside. That's also not getting into the problems that comes with being immortal yet having loved ones who are not.<br /> <br /> In terms of playable immortals, Prometheans, barring accidents, can live for an exceedingly long time in their path to become human, and Vampires have an equally long lifespan if they can avoid the problems of Hunters, the sun and, of course, each other. However, Prometheans can never stay in the same place without ruining the world around them, nor can Vampires just enjoy themselves with their own kin because of how cut-throat Vampire society is. However, both still need to eat, quite regularly, and both have significant weaknesses in exchange for their immortality (such as fire).<br /> <br /> As for high Wyrd Changelings, as noted, it's only Changelings who are Wyrd 10 that are at risk of becoming Gentry - you do not have to be very low Wyrd to avoid it. Further, there is a merit that actually grants the life extending bonuses of higher Wyrd while being lower Wyrd, though it doesn't grant bonuses past the maximum listed amount. Even if you never go past Wyrd 5, and don't invest in the merit, Changelings can live a very long and fulfilling life. Yes, they live with the fear that the Gentry will come and steal them away...but that's why Changelings form Freeholds, Courts and Motleys. There is safety in numbers, and by being changed by the Gentry you now have a whole new world to explore and marvel at, and at least now you're equiped with abilities that make you better able to withstand the world at large (far better than mortals can anyways).<br /> <br /> And if you really still want immortality as a Changeling? Isn't there an entitlement that grants something to that effect, or at least significantly prolonges one's age? I remember Baroness Nerak has one Changeling of the Autumn Court (Madam Spidertoes I believe) who has it, and she's described as being from an age before electric lights...<br /> <br /> Also, Charlaquin wasn't being insulting regarding playing Changeling Luke Skywalker - mechanically you can become Luke Skywalker in the game by being a Fairest Weisseu Frau with a sword Token that has the benefit of ignoring durability when striking objects and or people. What they were getting at is that if you want something in a game, just work it out with a GM and see how you can make it work without unbalancing everything. If you want immortality, make that a character arc for your character to discover. If you want to find or even become &quot;the one Good Gentry&quot;, then make that into the story of the chronicle - maybe the way to become a force comparable to the Gentry involves some secret deep within the Hedge and a great deal of permanent sacrifice, but in doing so you ascend to their level.<br /> <br /> Though it's not anywhere near ready, a Changeling Freehold I'm making has at least two Fae Touched in it, both with high positions, one being the wife of one King (the Paint Court) and one being the actual founder of a court (the Bone Court). The Paint King's wife manages to becme a proper Changeling by making a quick, but flawed deal with a Gentry whose Huntsman had captured here (it's meant to be a quest for players), whereas the Bone Queen wishes to become a Changeling herself in order to have mre time and capabilities to save her husband (another quest the player characters can indulge in). As of now, in the books, there is no explicite system for Fae Touched to become Changelings, but that doesn't mean that you can't make something up or work with a GM in order to make something, so long as it's interesting, balanced and, most of all, fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 12-04-2016, 01:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:44:55-08:00","id":1012069,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012053#post1012053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I do want to play empathetic characters and since becoming True Fae is out the question, I guess staying low powered (as in staying very low wyrd) and living in fear while dying old is the only option then?</div> </div> </div> </div>Err... As pointed out earlier in the thread, Wyrd 10 alone doesn't make you Fae. You also have to hit Wyrd 0, which really isn't that hard to avoid, especially since changelings can voluntarily lower their Wyrd when they need to. And if that's still an unacceptable level of risk for you, there are Merits that increase your effective Wyrd for the purposes of longevity, so you can live indefinitely without actually being at Wyrd 10. That said, living in fear is kind of par for the course in a Horror setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012053#post1012053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess it means that I have to become immortal through other means that doesn't involve the wyrd or faerie? Which means I have to use this <a href=\"http://&quot;http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Immortals&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">book</a> instead to look for other options if Changelings can follow through with it but if so, not only it won't feel the same but feels that being a Changeling is not even worth it afterall so why be one at all in the first place?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't understand this &quot;if my character can't have no-strings-attached immortality, why be one in the first place?&quot; attitude. But anyway, characters don't choose to become Changelings. Except in the sense that they choose to flee Arcadia, I guess, but they don't choose to be abducted. So the answer to &quot;why be one in the first place&quot; is, &quot;it beats being a prisoner of the Gentry for ever.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012053#post1012053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know this is a vieled insult but Luke Skywalker is just taking things too far since I believe that things in the game world have to make sense to the setting but then again though, the themes can restrict other possibilities that can along with it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was not intended to be an insult, I apologize if it was unintentionally insulting. Rather, I was trying to use hyperbole to illustrate that Dark Ages: Fae is a different setting than Changeling: the Lost. That doesn't mean you can't bring elements of one setting into another if you want to do that. In a tabletop RPG, you have the power and the freedom to change the setting to suit your taste, and if that means introducing characters from other settings, that's fine. Have fun the way you have fun.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012053#post1012053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes that's what I was referring to as PCs and if it's minigame then why bother? I guess it's a meaningless choice after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>You seem to consider a lot of things meaningless. To quote the Goblin King, &quot;you say that so often. I wonder what your basis for comparison is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T10:49:10-08:00","id":1012071,"title":"","content":"I believe what the general consensus is that changing the nature of the True Fae is possible, but you'd need to take creative liberty and change the default game state of Changeling: the Lost in order to do so. The True Fae were made to be solipsistic god-children-stories in order to evoke the feeling of the truly alien and inhuman, and in my opinion succeeded in a way that would shape all CofD gamelines afterwards, and by changing that one of the core elements of Changeling would be removed as well. <br /> <br /> Now, I do have two solutions to this predicament. But before that it sounds more like you're looking for an end-game for your Changeling character that would allow them to remain a part of the setting indefinitely. So I need to know for sure: Do you want a way to make your Changeling immortal but have them vaguely retain their mortal personality and values? (Because as Taidragon said, you must sacrifice something for immortality in CofD.) Or do you want a way to play as one of the True Fae but as a sympathetic and relatable character?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Spellcheck and Polish 12-04-2016, 01:53 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:11:57-08:00","id":1012076,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012071#post1012071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you want a way to make your Changeling immortal but have them vaguely retain their mortal personality and values? (Because as Taidragon said, you must sacrifice something for immortality in CofD.) Or do you want a way to play as one of the True Fae but as a sympathetic and relatable character?</div> </div> </div> </div>As for the Former yes and as for the Latter, if the &quot;True Fae&quot; are former changelings then shouldn't they be still be sympathetic and relatable as they were Changelings before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:28:06-08:00","id":1012080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012076#post1012076\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As for the Former yes and as for the Latter, if the &amp;quot;True Fae&amp;quot; are former changelings then shouldn't they be still be sympathetic and relatable as they were Changelings before?</div> </div> </div> </div>I believe I noted this earlier, but no, not really. Changelings and the True Fae are trapped in a cycle of abuse, power and vanity - Chaneglings are changed utterly by their experience in Arcadia, and even if it's not as terrible as some durances, a Changeling is still changed and given triggers that if, well, triggered, make them feel as they were in Arcadia instead of how they were as human. This is a type of insanity, and part of the reason that Wyrd 10 Clarity 0 Changelings go into the Hedge to become True Fae is because they believe not only that they're still in Arcadia, but that they have power comparable to their previous Keepers. In a sense, this is a case of Changelings empathizing with the Gentry, who are all mad, vain and self grandizing. A True Fae may have some familiar aspects to those who knew them as a Changeling, but in this case they have simply become what changed them in the first place.<br /> <br /> Part of pretty much every splat in Chronicles of Darkness has a familiar theme: with great power comes great sacrifice, and the potential for great insanity. Attaining a level of power that puts you even a little beyond human physically and mentally (that is, where you can start getting Attributes and Skills above 6) has you starting losing your fuel stat regularly, as well as having requirements beyond what low tier characters were required. This can end up changing the character significantly. Becoming a being like a True Fae, which seems to be what you're aiming for, would require a much greater change to them.<br /> <br /> Remember, True Fae have effectively divorced themselves from how they were as humans (or whatever they may once have been); they are utterly alien to the normal rules of society and reality. They make their own rules, and are effectively gods within their own domain (to the point that some are actually unkillable within it, no matter how desicated a corpse they leave behind). If you want to become a player version of that that is powerful and empathetic and relatable, something has to change, because you've effectively removed any downside of becoming a Gentry save that the non-empathetic ones will see you as a target even moreso than a Changeling would be.<br /> <br /> That mini-game mentioned above was about how the True Fae regularly fight to obtain the titles and names of other Gentry, as that boosts their considerable power further. Vampires are cutthroat, but Gentry are downright terrifying to one another. In that sense, it's not that bad staying as a Changeling - there's always a bigger fish to fry, after all, and what's bigger or juicier to a Fae than a coveted name/title belonging to a rival?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:28:59-08:00","id":1012081,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12524\" data-vbnamecard=\"12524\">Veindark</a>, gotcha.<br /> <br /> In that case option one is probably the best. And that's drawing upon the idea of becoming more than Changeling, but less than a True Fae.<br /> <br /> One of the most brilliant move of 2nd Edition is the idea of &quot;No Neat Boxes&quot;, as pioneered as often as possible to showcase the mystery and unknown of the setting. So if you want an immortal Changeling that completely fits within the horror core setting of CofD, then all you need to do is have them search for a means of transcending mortality without completely abandoning it. This won't be easy, in fact it'll be as difficult as following the Equinox Road back to Arcadia to confront your Keeper and gain some measure of closure for the torment your character endured. But it is possible.<br /> <br /> To just spit ball some in game ideas: The Hedge. The Hedge is already full of faerie creatures that lie somewhere between reality and Arcadia. If you said, &quot;my character is going to quest in the Hedge for a means of<br /> becoming an immortal Hobgoblin&quot; then I cannot imagine a single ST who wouldn't start salivating at the mouth (because as we know, all Story Tellers have an insatiable appetite for good stories.) <br /> <br /> Now, the catch is that in order to stay true to the setting you have to compromise a little for the sake of Changeling's themes of &quot;beautiful lies, painful truths.&quot; Yes, your character might not succeed and either become a monster or be recaptured. Yes, your character might succeed except in a way they weren't expecting. But that compromise allows all imagination to open up within the confines of the themes and moods of the setting. <br /> <br /> And that's all I've got. Hope it helps. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> (P.S. As for the latter, I'm going to have to agree with Taidragon again. The only way to play the Gentry is as inhuman fantasy settings that walk and talk. The only way to play a sympathetic True Fae is to play an Exile. Those banished from Arcadia and with barely the powers above a Changeling or Hobgoblin. Their disconnect from Arcadia forces upon them human concepts, and is the only time they come close to genuine human thoughts and feelings.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3436,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","user":"Dusksage","date":".  Polish 12-04-2016, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3436_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T11:48:12-08:00","id":1012087,"title":"","content":"*Comes in to see what the problem is*<br /> <br /> Oh. It's one of those problems.<br /> <br /> *walks back out*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:33:31-08:00","id":1012106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012053#post1012053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes that's what I was referring to as PCs and if it's minigame then why bother? I guess it's a meaningless choice after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>It represent's a pretty spectacular choice for your changeling. To use an easy if uneven example, it's if Luke joined the Dark Side. True Fae aren't the Dark Side, but it's subverting the tradition of protagonists being pure of intent and overcoming petty character traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T12:41:36-08:00","id":1012111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dusksage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012081#post1012081\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, the catch is that in order to stay true to the setting you have to compromise a little for the sake of Changeling's themes of &quot;beautiful lies, painful truths.&quot; Yes, your character might not succeed and either become a monster or be recaptured. Yes, your character might succeed except in a way they weren't expecting. But that compromise allows all imagination to open up within the confines of the themes and moods of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then why bother playing Changeling at all? It's after all a meaningless/hopeless game with little or no reward.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-04-2016, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:07:20-08:00","id":1012120,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012111#post1012111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then why bother playing Changeling at all? It's after all a meaningless/hopeless game with little or no reward.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, first of all: horror game. You play it for the catharsis of experiencing the horrific in a safe environment. Second of all, just because you can't become immortal without some kind of compromise doesn't mean there's no hope. Changeling is one of the most hopeful, if not <i>the</i> most hopeful game in Chronicles of Darkness, although Promethean is another top contender for that title. It's just that what you hope for isn't no-strings-attached immortality. It's simpler things, like security, belonging, acceptance. If you think a game is meaningless unless it can be used to fill the very specific power fantasy of immortality without drawbacks, you'renotb going to find much meaning in Chronicles of Darkness games. At least, not without some serious setting and rules hacks. Again, if you think that Changeling game would be fun, you can play that Changeling game. But it's not the Game Lost sets out to be, so you'll need to spill some ink if you want to make Lost that game at your table.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:28:15-08:00","id":1012128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012120#post1012120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, first of all: horror game. You play it for the catharsis of experiencing the horrific in a safe environment. Second of all, just because you can't become immortal without some kind of compromise doesn't mean there's no hope. Changeling is one of the most hopeful, if not <i>the</i> most hopeful game in Chronicles of Darkness, although Promethean is another top contender for that title. It's just that what you hope for isn't no-strings-attached immortality. It's simpler things, like security, belonging, acceptance. If you think a game is meaningless unless it can be used to fill the very specific power fantasy of immortality without drawbacks, you'renotb going to find much meaning in Chronicles of Darkness games. At least, not without some serious setting and rules hacks. Again, if you think that Changeling game would be fun, you can play that Changeling game. But it's not the Game Lost sets out to be, so you'll need to spill some ink if you want to make Lost that game at your table.</div> </div> </div> </div>Although simple things like acceptance, belonging and security are more like short term goals that may not last which still doesn't change the fact you're still living in fear and ultimately dying of old age never realizing your true extent as a Changeling while immortality is more a long term goal that at least makes everything you did actually worth it so it's kinda ironic that you call Changeling the &quot;most hopeful game&quot; without considering those prospects which is where I see deep down inside, Changeling still defaults itself into hopelessness which it takes form of a dilemma without offering a third option at hand.<br /> <br /> So in short, if the dilemma has it where the only choice I have is either die in old age never realizing my true extent as a Changeling or becoming Immortal by becoming a True Fae which also means sacrificing your empathy and compassion becoming the very abusive monster that you've feared and been fighting against this whole time which the cycle only repeats itself then what's the point of everything at all? That's my main point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-04-2016, 04:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:33:49-08:00","id":1012132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012128#post1012128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although simple things like acceptance, belonging and security are more like short term goals that may not last which still doesn't change the fact you're still living in fear and ultimately dying of old age never realizing your true extent as a Changeling while immortality is more a long term goal that at least makes everything you did actually worth it so it's kinda ironic that you call Changeling the &amp;quot;most hopeful game&amp;quot; without considering those prospects which is where I see deep down inside, Changeling still defaults itself into hopelessness which it takes form of a dilemma without offering a third option at hand.</div> </div> </div> </div>There are unlimited options, but there are no options that are completely free of consequences. Immortality is entirely achievable in Changeling if you want that, but you won't get it without [i]some[i] kind of sacrifice. Again, if that makes it meaningless to you, you're not going to find meaning in CofD as-written. Sorry.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:37:40-08:00","id":1012135,"title":"","content":"Why do you need to be immortal for anything to be &quot;worth it&quot;? Changelings can live for centuries. You're never going to play through that much time in-game unless you start skipping huge portions. <br /> <br /> Becoming a True Fae doesn't even help there. A Gentry isn't really the changeling they once were. They treat identities like outfits. One can be kind and benevolent in one title and a ruthless tyrant in another at the same time. They could even have one fight the other, if they got bored.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:42:23-08:00","id":1012139,"title":"","content":"Simple things like acceptance, belonging and security is the basis of mental health and happiness in people, and dying of old age is among the least awful ways to go. If you manage all that you've lived a very meaningful and happy life.<br /> I do get that Changelings are not like humans, but Changelings starts out recently escaped abuse victims. To fulfil those goals must be so much more rewarding for a Changeling than for many people who grow up taking most of those things for granted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/410713/Bloodlines-The-Ageless\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Ageless</a> and <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/491569/Fire--Revolution-Carthians\" target=\"_blank\">Fire &amp; Revolution: Carthians</a> on STV<br /> Some other stuff I've done: Ordo Dracul Mysteries: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1138490-idea-coil-of-owls?p=1140522\" target=\"_blank\">Mystery of Smoke</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1227848-mystery-of-%C5%BEiva-house-rule-revision\" target=\"_blank\">Revised Mystery of \u017diva</a> Mage The Awakening: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/0B2LMDRtfCcpdZDU1dWJzT1dNeEE/view\" target=\"_blank\">Spell Quick Reference</a> (single page and landscape for computer screens)","edited":{"userid":11887,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","user":"Tessie","date":".  Spelling 12-04-2016, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11887-tessie","name":"Tessie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11887_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:46:06-08:00","id":1012142,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012128#post1012128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although simple things like acceptance, belonging and security are more like short term goals that may not last which still doesn't change the fact you're still living in fear and ultimately dying of old age never realizing your true extent as a Changeling while immortality is more a long term goal that at least makes everything you did actually worth it so it's kinda ironic that you call Changeling the &quot;most hopeful game&quot; without considering those prospects which is where I see deep down inside, Changeling still defaults itself into hopelessness which it takes form of a dilemma without offering a third option at hand.<br /> <br /> So in short, if the dilemma has it where the only choice I have is either die in old age never realizing my true extent as a Changeling or becoming Immortal by becoming a True Fae which also means sacrificing your empathy and compassion becoming the very abusive monster that you've feared and been fighting against this whole time which the cycle only repeats itself then what's the point of everything at all? That's my main point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is &quot;realizing your true extent as a Changeling&quot; such a central goal for you? I don't mean that dismissively, I'm genuinely curious. If we have a better idea why that is so important from your perspective we may be able to offer better answers to what you're asking.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:47:43-08:00","id":1012144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012128#post1012128\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Although simple things like acceptance, belonging and security are more like short term goals that may not last which still doesn't change the fact you're still living in fear and ultimately dying of old age never realizing your true extent as a Changeling while immortality is more a long term goal that at least makes everything you did actually worth it so it's kinda ironic that you call Changeling the &quot;most hopeful game&quot; without considering those prospects which is where I see deep down inside, Changeling still defaults itself into hopelessness which it takes form of a dilemma without offering a third option at hand.<br /> <br /> So in short, if the dilemma has it where the only choice I have is either die in old age never realizing my true extent as a Changeling or becoming Immortal by becoming a True Fae which also means sacrificing your empathy and compassion becoming the very abusive monster that you've feared and been fighting against this whole time which the cycle only repeats itself then what's the point of everything at all? That's my main point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Outside of what Charlaquin has noted, Changelings have one massive benefit that not even the True Fae have - the ability to explore the nature between Fae and Human, use their own creativity to make new and unique things that can benefit others, and they can truly <i>marvel</i> at all that they have open to them. The Hedge is a dangerous place, full of terrible creatures, thorns, Arcadia and a truly nasty habit of revealing truths that you'd rather not face...but it's also filled with treasures even the Gentry covet, opportunities that can make you weep, and literal hopes and dreams Changelings can view and even assist with. They have suffered their durance, their masters may want them back at any cost and the world they've come back to isn't all sunshine and roses, but there is one truth for all Changelings: for all they have lost, they have truly gained something <i>more</i>. They have become the stuff of fairy tales, and while there may not be a Happily Ever After (again, as noted, horror game) you still can endeavor to make the world a better place for your own kind, if not others at large.<br /> <br /> That's how I see it anyways. This game isn't for everyone, but if you really see the above as &quot;pointless&quot;, I'm going to question just what you came to this game to achieve. This isn't about becoming an immortal god - the closest you can come to that is Mage, and even that has a massive number of pitfalls. As for what your &quot;true extent as a Changeling&quot; is, that's for you to decide. Again, as I said, stuff of fairy tales - be imaginative, be bold and show the horrors just what you are made of!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T13:59:54-08:00","id":1012154,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tessie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012139#post1012139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simple things like acceptance, belonging and security is the basis of mental health and happiness in people, and dying of old age is among the least awful ways to go. If you manage all that you've lived a very meaningful and happy life.<br /> I do get that Changelings are not like humans, but Changelings starts out recently escaped abuse victims. To fulfil those goals must be so much more rewarding for a Changeling than for many people who grow up taking most of those things for granted.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest I was never too comfortable with the entire abuse victim theme but I was looking into more into things focuses on Faerie aspects itself and it's esoteric ends.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012142#post1012142\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is &quot;realizing your true extent as a Changeling&quot; such a central goal for you? I don't mean that dismissively, I'm genuinely curious. If we have a better idea why that is so important from your perspective we may be able to offer better answers to what you're asking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simply because Changelings are not human and dying of old age is rather anticlimatic and depressing at the sametime while your character could be so much more than that.<br /> <br /> Or simply put it, being a Changeling has potential for transhumanism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012132#post1012132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There are unlimited options, but there are no options that are completely free of consequences. Immortality is entirely achievable in Changeling if you want that, but you won't get it without [i]some[i] kind of sacrifice. Again, if that makes it meaningless to you, you're not going to find meaning in CofD as-written. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Still kinda contradictory to pretend there are unlimited options in the face of a bipolar dilemma with the same outcome as I can see.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:07:18-08:00","id":1012161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012144#post1012144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This isn't about becoming an immortal god</div> </div> </div> </div>And this is where our main problem lies...<br /> <br /> If you take Buddhism or East Asian philosophies into account, becoming a immortal god is the goal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:15:21-08:00","id":1012168,"title":"","content":"I think we have the root of it. Changeling (and by extension, both the World of Darkness and the Chronicles of Darkness), are not Transhumanist in its core design or its design philosophy. Sure, they games might flirt with some of the concepts, but ultimately they come down to idea that the life you lead having more value than the fact that life will one day end. While you may not agree with this position (likely considering it death-ist as all hell), it is fairly deep to the core of the setting.<br /> <br /> But, we can't play these games without bring our own philosophies to the table, so if its that it important, its a relatively simple mechanical trick to grant a power or ability that grants functional immortality ,so you don't have to worry about it and can turn your attention to other things. But as a storyteller I would be more inclined to examine that fear of death and the idea of trying to find meaning in a ultimately nihilistic universe.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:18:26-08:00","id":1012170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012154#post1012154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest I was never too comfortable with the entire abuse victim theme but I was looking into more into things focuses on Faerie aspects itself and it's esoteric ends.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry you feel that way. Gonna make Changeling the Lost a hard game for you to enjoy.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012154#post1012154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Simply because Changelings are not human and dying of old age is rather anticlimatic and depressing at the sametime while your character could be so much more than that.<br /> <br /> Or simply put it, being a Changeling has potential for transhumanism.</div> </div> </div> </div>Finally, glad we can stop beating around the bush. Chronicles of Darkness is generally more humanist. If you're looking for transhumanist themes, the game as-written simply isn't going to cater to that desire. You can hack it if you want, or you can look elsewhere for your transhumanism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012154#post1012154\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Still kinda contradictory to pretend there are unlimited options in the face of a bipolar dilemma with the same outcome as I can see.</div> </div> </div> </div>Unlimited doesn't mean unconstrained. The set of all whole numbers doesn't contain any decimals, but it's still infinite. The options for endgame goals for Changeling characters do not include immortality without sacrifice, but they are still limitless. You have also failed to illustrate how the &quot;dilemma&quot; is in any way binary. We've been over the fact that you can easily play a Changeling with an unlimited lifespan without becoming Gentry, or even risking becoming so. So the dichotomy you've set up between &quot;become an unsympathetic alien monster or die of old age&quot; has already been demonstrated to be false. Just because you don't like any of the options doesn't mean there are only two of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:19:58-08:00","id":1012173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012161#post1012161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And this is where our main problem lies...<br /> <br /> If you take Buddhism or East Asian philosophies into account, becoming a immortal god is the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uhm. No. That is like the exact opposite of what Buddhism puts forward. It's certainly the opposite of Hinduism, has no place in Confucianism or Taoism, is a non-disucssion point in Shinto and-Look, nutshell, no.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Okay, in fairness, it depends on which school of Buddhism you're following-but even then, there's a difference in your ideas of becoming an immortal god and their ideas on the subject.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 12-04-2016, 06:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T14:21:30-08:00","id":1012175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012161#post1012161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And this is where our main problem lies...</div> </div> </div> </div>No, our problem lies in you not liking the core conceits of the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012161#post1012161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you take Buddhism or East Asian philosophies into account, becoming a immortal god is the goal.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's a pretty radical interpretation of Buddhism. But either way, Changeling the Lost is not Buddhism.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T21:41:34-08:00","id":1012377,"title":"","content":"Nothing in 2e core says anything about becoming a True Fae at Wyrd 10, it was an opinional rule in a previous edition.<br /> <br /> If you want your Changeling changeling be achieve wyrd 10, without turning into a True Fae, that appears to be the default assumption, that why immortal life span is listed, it would be no point in that if you just turned into a True Fae.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:19:20-08:00","id":1012392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012377#post1012377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nothing in 2e core says anything about becoming a True Fae at Wyrd 10, it was an opinional rule in a previous edition.<br /> <br /> If you want your Changeling changeling be achieve wyrd 10, without turning into a True Fae, that appears to be the default assumption, that why immortal life span is listed, it would be no point in that if you just turned into a True Fae.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I actually prefer the True Fae not being ex-changelings, it takes away the mystery of what True Fae actually are.<br /> <br /> So I guess I rather have it that Changelings can't become True Fae because they're not True Fae no matter how high their Wyrd is, since I kinda prefer the True Fae being never human in the first place which they're truly alien anomalious beings and sort of just &quot;popped into existence&quot; through unknown means although the True Fae can be tied into the Wyrd somehow however.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12524,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","user":"Veindark","date":". 12-05-2016, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:21:22-08:00","id":1012393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012392#post1012392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I actually prefer the True Fae not being ex-changelings, it takes away the mystery of what True Fae actually are.</div> </div> </div> </div>You appear to be laboring under the impression that &quot;changelings can become True Fae&quot; means &quot;all True Fae were once changelings.&quot; This is not the case and never has been.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:27:03-08:00","id":1012397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012393#post1012393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You appear to be laboring under the impression that &quot;changelings can become True Fae&quot; means &quot;all True Fae were once changelings.&quot; This is not the case and never has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that certain conclusion has been implied if you follow that logic and putting two and two together along with fringe horrors of the True Fae &quot;reproduction cycle&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:27:47-08:00","id":1012398,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012393#post1012393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You appear to be laboring under the impression that &quot;changelings can become True Fae&quot; means &quot;all True Fae were once changelings.&quot; This is not the case and never has been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus, it logically cannot be true of all true fae. Since changelings are created by the actions of true fae.... so if all true fae were originally changelings there never would have been a changeling because there was never a changeling in the first place because there wasn't a true fae, etc. etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:34:35-08:00","id":1012402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012398#post1012398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, it logically cannot be true of all true fae. Since changelings are created by the actions of true fae.... so if all true fae were originally changelings there never would have been a changeling because there was never a changeling in the first place because there wasn't a true fae, etc. etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Which is why I think Changelings and True Fae should be separate beings entirely.<br /> <br /> I think we could also go to the &quot;DA: Fae&quot; route saying that the Arcadia were originally one with Earth and the True Fae used to Walk and dominate the Earth in ages past (during the Antiquity and Middle Ages) as the &quot;Firstborn&quot; until it was separated in modern ages with the creation of the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12524-veindark","name":"Veindark","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"248"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:36:46-08:00","id":1012404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012397#post1012397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought that certain conclusion has been implied if you follow that logic and putting two and two together along with fringe horrors of the True Fae &quot;reproduction cycle&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Putting two and two together is &quot;any Fae might have, in theory, once been a changeling, because any changeling could theoretically go on to become a Fae.&quot; That's not &quot;they're all made out of changelings,&quot; that's &quot;This could be your Monarch twenty years from now.&quot;<br /> <br /> Your &quot;certain conclusion&quot; operates on the logic that pyromaniacs are the sole source of house fires.<br /> <br /> Becoming a True Fae means you stop being a person in favor of being a <i>personality.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:38:31-08:00","id":1012405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012397#post1012397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought that certain conclusion has been implied if you follow that logic and putting two and two together along with fringe horrors of the True Fae &quot;reproduction cycle&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>In this case, the implication is wrong. Honestly, too many changelings die in mundane ways or get taken back prior to that point for it to count as a &quot;reproduction cycle&quot;. There's honestly always been too many True Fae for that to be the angle. And again, even those who reach Wyrd 10 basically have to let go of the rope to really be fucked.<br /> <br /> Becoming Nightmare is more the natural consequence of a person who's so afraid of living in an uncertain world where safety can't be guarenteed and happiness is a pursuit rather than a promise, when wish fulfillment is not a struggle but something to handed to them-when a chick decides it's better to hatch into an egg rather than the other way around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-04T22:43:08-08:00","id":1012407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012402#post1012402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Which is why I think Changelings and True Fae should be separate beings entirely.</div> </div> </div> </div>They are. It just happens that through rare circumstances it might be possible for changelings to cast off their humanity and become a true being of narrative, an opportunity only have because of how their torn up souls are filled with glamour and fables.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think we could also go to the &quot;DA: Fae&quot; route saying that the Arcadia were originally one with Earth and the True Fae used to Walk and dominate the Earth in ages past (during the Antiquity and Middle Ages) as the &quot;Firstborn&quot; until it was separated in modern ages with the creation of the Hedge. </div> </div> </div>There is no reason why that cannot be true in your CofD games, the history of supernaturals is generally rather obscured so you can decide to do things like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-05T01:50:46-08:00","id":1012453,"title":"","content":"&quot;Wait, were you human once?&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;I have <i>memories</i> of being human. They might not be <i>mine.&quot;</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:01:27-08:00","id":1014034,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1012405#post1012405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Becoming Nightmare is more the natural consequence of a person who's so afraid of living in an uncertain world where safety can't be guarenteed and happiness is a pursuit rather than a promise, when wish fulfillment is not a struggle but something to handed to them-when a chick decides it's better to hatch into an egg rather than the other way around.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I love you for that quote, but I also have to hate you since once again you have forced into my brain &quot;If it cannot break out of its shell, a chick will die without ever truly being born, etc.&quot;. Not that I don't love Utena, mind you, but....dammit, its worse than a song stuck in your head, you know!<br /> <br /> Not even gonna get into the parallels of being true fae versus Akio abilities, manipulations, and goals. We'd be here all day.<br /> <br /> Ahem. Changeling-turned-Gentry and resultant empathy question! <br /> <br /> &quot;You want to maintain your old personality? How? Why? When you start to dream, do you in the dream worry about things happening in the waking world? When you wake up from a dream, are you able to maintain concerns for and the personality from your dreaming mind? Would you even care or think to try? Because that's the divide between who you were as a changeling and who you are as a True Fae! But fine. Say you ARE empathetic, that you retain some semblance of human morality! Congrats! You are now a True Fae with a sense of right and wrong! By the way, all your neighbors are sociopaths who want to eat you! But they have rules, too. They only get to eat you if they beat you in a game of chess! Oops, turns out those pieces are alive. Better keeps those pawns out of harm's way, since you care about these sorts of things. Be immoral to hurt the opposing pieces, too. Good luck winning with that retained sense of compassion you got there, bud. Or you can steal some folk from the living world. Make them act out a story for you. Why would you do that? What a silly question. Why do humans breath the air? Drink the water? Eat the food? To survive, of course. Stories are your lifeblood, friend. Whether you tell them yourself or allow them to unfold around you, so long as they are being told the Wyrd will weave its Fate and your existence is secure. What happens if you let the stories stop? What a stupid question. Then you die. Yes, yes, yes. Happily ever after. Of course its true. For them. The mortals. For you, the tale itself....ever after is just a pretty way of saying THE END. Finale. No more to come. Death. Worse than death, really. Human death promises the hope of some kind of afterlife. Maybe. You have no such hope. The end for you is the end. But it doesn't have to be that way. You just need to collect a few...props. Its okay. You were like them once. And look where you are now. They can take it. Heh. Look at it this way. The Wyrd wants you to write the next great Arcadian novel, and it has a strict deadline for publication, and all you can think about is how sad it is that some ink and paper have to be used up to get the job done. You are a True Fae now. You have greater concerns.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T16:06:50-08:00","id":1014037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1014034#post1014034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, I love you for that quote, but I also have to hate you since once again you have forced into my brain &quot;If it cannot break out of its shell, a chick will die without ever truly being born, etc.&quot;. Not that I don't love Utena, mind you, but....dammit, its worse than a song stuck in your head, you know!</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-size:8px\">zettai<br /> unmei<br /> mokushiroku</span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-07T17:07:36-08:00","id":1014057,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nothri</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1014034#post1014034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or you can steal some folk from the living world. Make them act out a story for you. Why would you do that? What a silly question. Why do humans breath the air? Drink the water? Eat the food? To survive, of course. Stories are your lifeblood, friend. Whether you tell them yourself or allow them to unfold around you, so long as they are being told the Wyrd will weave its Fate and your existence is secure. What happens if you let the stories stop? What a stupid question. Then you die. Yes, yes, yes. Happily ever after. Of course its true. For them. The mortals. For you, the tale itself....ever after is just a pretty way of saying THE END. Finale. No more to come. Death. Worse than death, really. Human death promises the hope of some kind of afterlife. Maybe. You have no such hope. The end for you is the end.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well.<br /> <br /> Let's be totally clear, here: You're dead already.<br /> <br /> The sun has set on your mortal days, and \u2014 <i>Et in Arcadia ego</i> \u2014 the Wyrd stands before you in the full aspect of the Harvest itself. The only thing standing between you and blind oblivion \u2014 all that permits you even a shred of a chance at a new game \u2014 is that Fate likes a good scary story on the endless nights when the paths between the worlds are short and straight. Even in the timeless realm of Faerie a prisoner is entitled to the prospect of freedom \u2014 the Strangers didn't make the rule of there always being a catch, but they gladly take advantage where they can.<br /> <br /> You're a ghost trying to fend off the Reaper for long enough that your unfinished business is concluded, your deepest wish granted, your discontented soul freed from the Hell of jewels and thorns that bars you from the ultimate fulfillment of the desires you so desperately pursue. You're racing against time, seeking to hasten the Dawn's arrival before you fall asleep for the final time in the temptingly soft space between suffering.<br /> <br /> You use any means possible to beat back the cessation of your adventures \u2014 while the end is coming no matter what you do, the nature of your Durance demands the possibility of an ending you can be happy with. You know it must exist, because hope and faith, like trust and fellow-feeling, are among the only luxuries not afforded to you \u2014 leaving anything to chance is to place it in the hands of your sole jailer and executioner, and you cannot know why It does this or what terrors It has in store for you in the great Nothing after life.<br /> <br /> And so you sit in the middle of the night on All Hallow's Eve, a lonely soul playing the part of Scheherazade, Dead-Clever Bride of the Wyrd. Arrangements will be made if you need anything to tell your stories, but compelling subjects do not grow on trees, even here in the wonderland on the edge of dreams, so you are sadly bound to inconvenience someone eventually, whether you venture through the woods to get the goods yourself or enlist a wandering river or a rolling stone for aid.<br /> <br /> In any case, before you die, the way out is through. (Farewell, good hunter. May you find your worth in the waking world.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-09T12:54:32-08:00","id":1014901,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Veindark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1011699#post1011699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well say if I pick the True Fae decision, I wonder how they can maintain being themselves (or the the essence of you)</div> </div> </div> </div>Zero Clarity. Think of what that phrase means not in context of mechanics of a game we play but just plain English. Now picture a being with zero clarity with unlimited power to reshape anything in its own little pocket universe realm. Experiencing empathy has accurate perception of others as a prerequisite after all and I challenge you to provide an example where it is otherwise, because all my attempts fail. See <a href=\"https://www.google.com/search?q=empathy+vs+sympathy&amp;ie=utf-8&amp;oe=utf-8\" target=\"_blank\">Empathy vs Sympathy</a>. Zero Clarity is amazing word craft in the game mechanics to capture the idea that it represents.<br /> <br /> How can you have an accurate sense of self when you have no accurate senses at all? You can't. By being completely without any Clarity is the dissolution of the self as a meaningful construct and there is no 'you' at that time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><i>\u201cYouth ages, immaturity is outgrown, ignorance can be educated, and drunkenness sobered, but stupid lasts forever.\u201d </i>~ <b>Aristophanes</b><br /> <i>&quot;Virescit Vulnere Virtus&quot;</i> ~ <b>Stewart Clan Motto</b></div> <div align=\"center\"><span style=\"font-size:18px\"><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Frailty Chronicles</a></span><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">;</a><b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/801713-homebrew-of-pale_crusader\" target=\"_blank\">Understanding the power of limitations.</a></b></div>","edited":{"userid":3279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","user":"Pale_Crusader","date":". 12-09-2016, 04:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3279-pale_crusader","name":"Pale_Crusader","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:15:24-08:00","id":1015286,"title":"","content":"It seems not even the Gentry are immune to the overarching rule of Changeling; for a great boon comes a proportional suffering and sacrifice. If anything, they have mastered and enforcered it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T10:56:44-08:00","id":1015307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1011669-non-abusive-empathetic-true-fae-even-possible-and-wyrd-10-changelings?p=1014057#post1014057\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Stuff</div> </div> </div> </div>Hot damn, Satch, ya' givin' me chills!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-10T14:12:15-08:00","id":1015368,"title":"","content":"hmmm..This thread has traveled pretty far (with a bunch of ideas I am going to use to torment my players), but think the heart of the OP's question was &quot;Can I have immortality and unlimited power without paying any of those nagging lose-your-soul costs?&quot; To which I would say &quot;No&quot;.<br /> Everyone who plays the game is welcome to do with it as they see fit, from setting, to themes, to mechanics, but as the Chronicles of Darkness is set up, Death is Real, Consequences are Real, Sacrifices are Real, Monsters are Real (and you a likely to be that Monster, or to be its Prey). If you find that you are unable to accept any of the concepts presented above, you may be better served either playing something more to tastes, or spilling a little ink to remake the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"