":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:24:52-08:00","id":1021037,"title":"","content":"Haven't read all of the thread yet, but to <b>Veindark</b>.<br /> <br /> Sources can be found here:<br /> <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/chroniclesofdarkness/changelingthelost/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/category/worl...gelingthelost/</a><br /> <br /> In the <b>Merits </b>document there are 2 merits you can look at to live a long time as a high clarity Changeling.<br /> Im not going to quote all of the texts, just mentioning relevant parts.<br /> <br /> Forever and a Day (\u2022)<br /> Effect: Double her Wyrd for the purposes of determining her lifespan (see p. XX). This cannot take her effective<br /> Wyrd beyond ten dots.<br /> <br /> Long of Days (\u2022\u2022)<br /> Effect: Some portion of the Gentry\u2019s agelessness has rubbed off on you, and you not feel time\u2019s<br /> passage as a mortal might. In some<br /> Lost, this manifests immediately. In others, it waits until a specific age and either slows, or<br /> ceases entirely.<br /> <br /> In the <b>Contracts </b>document there is a Contract that lets you de-age yourself and others by taking a walk through the Hedge.<br /> <br /> Flickering Hours (\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> Selecting the right trods, you alter the passage of time for yourself and any companions while in<br /> the Hedge.<br /> Cost: 2 Glamour for the changeling alone, 2 Glamour + 1 Willpower for a group<br /> \u2022 Fairest: The Fairest ages or rejuvenates herself and/or her subjects by one year when using this<br /> Contract. This effect is permanent.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Edit</b>: Finished reading the Thread. The discussion did not go where I expected. Also, <b>Veindark </b>is banned?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11799,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","user":"RBAWintrow","date":". 12-22-2016, 06:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11799-rbawintrow","name":"RBAWintrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11799_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"68"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T16:07:35-08:00","id":1021061,"title":"","content":"As of now, Veindark is banned. I don't know why. I did see a warning in another post from a mod, but it is probably a bad idea and in bad taste to discuss it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}